WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Pronunciation.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Careful listeners will notice many subtle differences between the sounds of Tamil and those of English.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.500
We concentrate here on features of pronunciation that are vital for clear understanding.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:19.500
One very important distinction in the sounds of Tamil is that between long and short vowels.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:25.500
In the Roman transcription we use, the long vowels are indicated by double letters.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:32.500
So that you may hear and learn to make these distinctions, listen to and repeat the following pairs of words.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.500
The word for 10.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.000
பத்து (pattu)

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.500
The word for look.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.000
பாரு (paaru)

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.500
The word for small.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.000
சின்ன (sinna)

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The word for fish.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
மீன் (miin)

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The word for salt.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.000
உப்பு (uppu)

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.000
The word for town.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
ஊரு (uuru)

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
The word for price.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.500
விலை (vela)

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.500
The word for work.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.500
வேலை (veela)

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.500
The word for one.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.500
ஒரு (oru)

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.500
The word for run.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.000
ஓடு (oodu)